	(text_box "PARTS AND THEIR JOBS\nJ201: USB-C socket (USB 2.0) on the right board edge: programming, the configurator and USB power.\nR207, R208: 5.1k pull-downs on CC1/CC2: they tell a USB-C charger or PC that a device is plugged in, so it turns on 5 V.\nU203: USBLC6-2SC6: ESD protection for D+ and D-. Its VBUS pin (5) takes the fused VBUS. Place it right at J201.\nF201: 0.5 A resettable fuse in USB VBUS (VBUS_IN -> VBUS): protects the PC's USB port and the board.\nC208: 1 uF on VBUS, at U203 pin 5.\nD201: B5819W Schottky diode: USB feeds +5V through it, and it stops the board 5 V flowing back into the PC. The 5V buck feeds +5V through its own diode (D101), so either source can run the board.\nU204: AMS1117-3.3 regulator: makes +3V3 (up to 1 A) from +5V for the whole board.\nC205, C206, C207: 10 uF on U204 input (pin 3); 22 uF and 100 nF on its output (pin 2). It needs them close to stay stable.\nU202: CH340C USB-to-serial converter (no crystal needed): joins the PC to the ESP32 UART0 (GPIO1 TX, GPIO3 RX).\nC204: 100 nF decoupling for U202 VCC (pin 16).\nR213: 0 R: ties U202 V3 (pin 4) to +3V3, so the CH340C runs at 3.3 V like the ESP32.\nR203, R204: 470 R in the UART0 lines (CH_TXD -> U0RXD, U0TXD -> CH_RXD): limit the current if both sides drive at once.\nQ201, Q202, R205, R206: auto-program: the PC (esptool) uses the DTR and RTS lines to pull EN low (reset) or IO0 low (boot mode); when DTR = RTS both are released. 10k base resistors.\nD202, R209: PWR LED (red): on while +3V3 is up, about 1.3 mA through 1k.\nD203, R210: STATUS LED (yellow) on GPIO2 (LED_STATUS), 1k."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 205 0)
		(size 192 40.9)
		(margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f4af76a9-6a1a-59aa-82ee-0867fa9540ae")
	)
	(text_box "PARTS AND THEIR JOBS\nU201: ESP32-WROOM-32E-N4: dual-core processor, 4 MB flash, Wi-Fi and Bluetooth; its antenna sticks out past the top board edge. GPIO34, 35, 36, 39 are inputs only. GPIO36 and GPIO39 dip low for about 80 ns when the ADC powers up (errata), so only VIN_SENSE and IMU_INT use them. NC pins: not used.\nC201, C202: 10 uF and 100 nF decoupling for U201 VDD (pin 2): Wi-Fi transmit bursts draw several hundred mA.\nR201, C203: 10k pull-up and 1 uF on EN: they hold the ESP32 in reset for roughly 10 ms (10k x 1 uF) after +3V3 comes up.\nSW201: RESET button: pulls EN low, the ESP32 restarts.\nR202: 10k pull-up on IO0: the ESP32 starts the firmware (IO0 high at reset).\nSW202: BOOT button: hold it while pressing RESET to start the USB bootloader by hand.\nR102, C101: VIN_SENSE: with R101 (100k, VIN input module) R102 (5.6k) divides the supply by 18.9 (30 V -> 1.59 V) for GPIO36 (ADC1); C101 (100 nF) filters it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 212 205 0)
		(size 192 22.45)
		(margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "db93af2b-547e-5989-adf7-ceee6b377edd")
	)
